vation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["HS2-HIS-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Assemble a cultures and communities showcase using the checklist. Check that you have permission for every personal item. Write a one-minute talk and two questions for further study. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Culture web: parts of culture; origin map: places in a story; greeting chart: language diversity; respect plan: living together fairly. Reasoning: I used review by attending to culture and explain why it matters rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: A display of flags and food pictures with no sources or permission shows stereotypes rather than understanding. Correction: Culture web: parts of culture; origin map: places in a story; greeting chart: language diversity; respect plan: living together fairly. Why: the correction restores accurate use of review.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: A display of flags and food pictures with no sources or permission shows stereotypes rather than understanding. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating review on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with review, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Culture web: parts of culture; origin map: places in a story; greeting chart: language diversity; respect plan: living together fairly. 